Postman Collection Outline

You can create a Postman collection named `ProductAPI` with the following endpoints:

| Method | Endpoint                          | Description                  |
|--------|-----------------------------------|------------------------------|
| POST   | `/products`                       | Create a product             |
| GET    | `/products`                       | List all products            |
| GET    | `/products/{id}`                  | Get product by ID            |
| PUT    | `/products/{id}`                  | Update product               |
| DELETE | `/products/{id}`                  | Delete product               |
| GET    | `/products/{id}/stock?count=5`    | Check stock availability     |
| GET    | `/products/sorted`                | Get products sorted by price |
| POST   | `/products`                       | Add multiple products        |
| GET    | `/products/range?start=0&end=5`   | Fetch range of products      |

Each request should include:
- Header: `Content-Type: application/json`
- Body (for POST/PUT): JSON with `name`, `description`, `price`, `quantity`

1. Create Products
	- Method: POST
	- URL: `http://localhost:9090/products`
	- Json eg: 
			{
			  "name": "Wireless Mouse",
			  "description": "Ergonomic mouse with USB receiver",
			  "price": 29.99,
			  "quantity": 50
			}

2. List All Products
    - Method: GET
    - URL: `http://localhost:9090/products`
    - output eg:
		    [
			    {
			        "id": 1,
			        "name": "Wireless Mouse",
			        "description": "Ergonomic mouse with USB receiver",
			        "price": 29.99,
			        "quantity": 50
			    },
			    {
			        "id": 2,
			        "name": "Gaming Laptop",
			        "description": "High-performance laptop for gaming",
			        "price": 1499.99,
			        "quantity": 10
			    }
			]

3. Get by Product id
	- Method: GET
    - URL: `http://localhost:9090/products/1`
    - output eg:
            {
                "id": 1,
                "name": "Wireless Mouse",
                "description": "Ergonomic mouse with USB receiver",
                "price": 29.99,
                "quantity": 50
            }

4. Update product
    - Method: PUT
    - URL: `http://localhost:9090/products/1`
    - Json eg:
            {
              "name": "Wireless Mouse Pro",
              "description": "Ergonomic mouse with USB receiver and extra buttons",
              "price": 39.99,
              "quantity": 40
            }
 
 5. Delete product
     - Method: DELETE
     - URL: `http://localhost:9090/products/1`

6. Check Stock Availability
    - Method: GET
    - URL: `http://localhost:9090/products/2/stock?count=5`
    - output eg:
            {
                "available": true
            }

7. Get Products Sorted by Price
